<section class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 py-16">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-6 text-center">How to Download Instagram Reels on iPhone</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 text-center mb-10">Last updated: <%= currentYear %></p>

    <div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
        Instagram Reels are short, engaging videos that are perfect for inspiration, tutorials, and entertainment. If you want to save a Reel to your iPhone for offline viewing, you can do it directly from Safari without installing any third-party app.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">Step 1: Copy the Reel link</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">Open the Instagram app, tap the three dots on a Reel, and select <strong>Copy link</strong>. The URL will look like <code>https://www.instagram.com/reel/CODE</code>.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">Step 2: Open Safari and paste the URL</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">Go to <a href="/" class="text-sky-600 dark:text-sky-400 hover:underline"><%= siteTitle %></a> in Safari. Paste the link into the input box and tap <strong>Get Video</strong>.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">Step 3: Choose a format</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">For Instagram Reels, MP4 is the best choice. Pick the MP4 format that matches the original quality. Tap the download card.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">Step 4: Save to Photos or Files</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">After the download starts, tap the file in the Safari downloads manager. You can then save it to your Photos app or Files app for easy access.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">Important copyright reminder</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">Only download Reels you created or have permission to save. Reposting or sharing someone else's Reel without credit can violate Instagram's Terms and copyright.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">Tips for iPhone users</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
        <li>Use Safari for the most reliable download experience.</li>
        <li>If the file does not open, use the Files app to locate it.</li>
        <li>Low storage? Download in a lower resolution if available.</li>
        <li>Keep your iOS updated for the best browser compatibility.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <details class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 p-4">
          <summary class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white cursor-pointer">Can I download private Reels?</summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 text-sm">Private Reels can only be downloaded by the account owner or with explicit permission.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 p-4">
          <summary class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white cursor-pointer">Do I need an app?</summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 text-sm">No. <%= siteTitle %> works directly in Safari on iPhone.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 p-4">
          <summary class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white cursor-pointer">Is there a watermark?</summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 text-sm">The downloaded file usually does not contain the Instagram Reels interface overlay.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
